# Render scratch: frame grid, captured audio, narration, timing log.
video/
trim.json
framescan/

# The finished videos. Tracked at first, when they were the thing being reviewed;
# now they are rewritten by every scheduled run, so a tracked copy only means the
# working tree is dirty on every run and the run has to choose between committing
# 60MB of binary nobody reads and leaving the tree unclean. They are reproducible
# from the source in this directory, which is the part worth keeping.
cookie_strateger_short.mp4
cookie_strateger_short.webm
cookie_strateger_long.mp4
cookie_strateger_long.webm
# Review stills written by `node director.mjs shots`.
beat_*.png

# youtube/posted.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, back when this ran in
# one long-lived container and the file could just stay on disk. A scheduled
# workflow gets a clean runner every time, so an untracked file is an empty one:
# the picker would find no history, fall back to the first cut, and post the same
# one every day. It is committed for the same reason it exists.
youtube/snapshot.log

# 外部レビューが開くフレームと、その判定。どちらもこの take 限りのもの。
# 判定は mp4 の sha256 に焼き付いているので、次の take では無効になる ——
# 追跡すると「前回の合格」が残っているように見えて紛らわしい。
review/
youtube/review-verdict.json
